cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper it accompanies
  (see preferred-citation below). Licensing is not uniform across this archive:
  the code is MIT and the results, derived data and laboratory notebooks are
  CC BY 4.0, but the manuscript in docs/papers/ is under copyright with no reuse
  licence granted. LICENSES.md sets out which terms apply where.
title: "Complements in the Queue: replication material"
abstract: >-
  The joint interconnection-allocation engine, the experiments behind
  "Complements in the Queue", and the numerical results they produced. The
  engine measures the residual - joint hosting capacity minus the best
  sequential study order - on distribution feeders, using an AC-verified
  Generalized-LinDistFlow instrument that certifies a feasible lower bound
  rather than a relaxation.
